# ~/.config/env/nvim.env — environment for nvim (monkey-nvim).
# The profiles source this file with `set -a`, so everything here reaches nvim
# and every process nvim starts. Add your own nvim-scoped variables anywhere in
# it: install.sh only touches the keys it seeds below (render_fill passes any
# other line through untouched), and a value already in the file always wins
# over the install-time environment (fill-empty), so hand edits survive
# re-runs. install.sh renders this template to the real file (0600) from the
# variables exported BEFORE the install ran. The file is independent of any
# other project's credential store.
#
# Seeded today: minuet-ai.nvim's provider variables, read by lua/ai.lua at nvim
# startup, and the proxy trio below, read not by lua but by the HTTP client
# minuet spawns. Empty means UNSET — a variable this file exports as empty
# reaches lua/ai.lua as nil, and lua/ai.lua registers a preset only when every
# variable of that preset is set. Neither the code nor this file carries
# defaults, so a half-filled set is a preset that does not exist, and a startup
# preset that does not exist leaves minuet unset up (keymaps included).
#
# Values are written bare; whitespace/quotes get auto-quoted on write.
# Keep this file free of newlines inside values — a newline breaks every
# KEY= line below it.

# ── minuet: master switch ──
# Preset that nvim activates at startup: local_fim | openai. Unset or empty
# = minuet is not set up at all (no AI completion, no keymaps); the installer
# writes this file and the profile line that sources it either way, every key
# empty, so the preset can be filled in by hand without another run.
NVIM_MINUET_PRESET=

# ── minuet: openai-compatible preset (needs ALL FOUR to be registered) ──
# NVIM_MINUET_BASE_URL is the prefix; lua/ai.lua appends /v1/chat/completions.
# NVIM_MINUET_MODEL is the model id exactly as the gateway expects it.
# NVIM_MINUET_NAME is the display name.
# The key itself is referenced by NAME (minuet's api_key is the variable name,
# read at request time), so no secret value lands in a rendered config.
NVIM_MINUET_API_KEY=
NVIM_MINUET_BASE_URL=
NVIM_MINUET_MODEL=
NVIM_MINUET_NAME=

# ── minuet: local FIM preset (needs ALL THREE to be registered) ──
# NVIM_MINUET_LOCAL_BASE_URL is the prefix; /v1/completions is appended.
# NVIM_MINUET_LOCAL_MODEL is the model id the server expects.
# NVIM_MINUET_LOCAL_NAME is the display name AND the request shape: only
# "llama.cpp" rewrites the call to llama.cpp's /infill endpoint
# (prompt/suffix -> input_prefix/input_suffix). Any other FIM server — Ollama,
# vLLM, LM Studio — must say so, because it keeps the plain /v1/completions
# request instead.
NVIM_MINUET_LOCAL_BASE_URL=
NVIM_MINUET_LOCAL_MODEL=
NVIM_MINUET_LOCAL_NAME=

# ── proxy ──
# The family-wide trio, named once in scripts/lib/env.sh (PROXY_ENV_KEYS) with
# the measured detail of which reader honours which spelling — read that
# before adding a fourth. Empty = unset, like every key above.
# minuet spawns curl, so a fresh install writes NO_PROXY with the loopback
# binds already merged in: the local FIM preset dials http://127.0.0.1:… and
# a proxy that fronts the gateway would otherwise swallow the local server
# too. Your own hand-set NO_PROXY always wins and is never rewritten.
# These three keys are the host's, not nvim's: the same names may be filled in
# again in another project's env file in this directory. render_fill never
# rewrites a non-empty line, so rotating a proxy means editing every file that
# lists them — and leaving them EMPTY here while another file holds a value is
# not neutral: this file is sourced later and an empty assignment clears the
# inherited value for everything nvim starts.
HTTPS_PROXY=
HTTP_PROXY=
NO_PROXY=
